<<<
all the time. The phrase is idiomatic English only when the time in question is a definite period fixed by the context, as in:—I did not see you because I was looking at her a. t. t. (that you were present);
===
**all the time.** The phrase is idiomatic English only when the time in question is a definite period fixed by the context, as in:—*I did not see you because I was looking at her a. t. t.* (that you were present);
>>>

